VeridianOS: fix compiler warnings in libplasma (drag events, thumbnail)

GCC reported:

- -Wdeprecated-declarations for the QDragEnterEvent and QDragMoveEvent
  constructors taking a QPoint, in Dialog::event()
  (src/plasmaquick/dialog.cpp) and EdgeEventForwarder::eventFilter()
  (src/plasmaquick/edgeeventforwarder.cpp). The forwarded position is
  computed as a QPointF and was rounded with toPoint() only to fit the Qt 5
  era constructor; it is now passed to the QPointF constructors directly.
  Dialog's QDropEvent forwarding rounded the same way (QDropEvent only has a
  QPointF constructor), so it is changed alike, keeping enter, move and drop
  in the same coordinates; EdgeEventForwarder already forwarded drops
  unrounded. The only difference is that forwarded drag positions keep
  their sub-pixel part.
- -Wunused-variable for 'm_renderStage' in
  WindowThumbnail::releaseResources()
  (src/declarativeimports/core/windowthumbnail.cpp). The local is used only
  by the GLX and EGL pixmap cleanup under HAVE_XCB_COMPOSITE; it is now
  declared under HAVE_XCB_COMPOSITE && (HAVE_GLX || HAVE_EGL), so builds
  without GLX and EGL do not declare it. Behaviour is unchanged.

diff -ru a/src/declarativeimports/core/windowthumbnail.cpp b/src/declarativeimports/core/windowthumbnail.cpp
--- a/src/declarativeimports/core/windowthumbnail.cpp	2026-10-08 17:09:10.645392903 -0400
+++ b/src/declarativeimports/core/windowthumbnail.cpp	2026-10-08 17:10:08.423538272 -0400
@@ -209,13 +209,15 @@
 
 void WindowThumbnail::releaseResources()
 {
-    QQuickWindow::RenderStage m_renderStage = QQuickWindow::NoStage;
     if (m_textureProvider) {
         window()->scheduleRenderJob(new DiscardTextureProviderRunnable(m_textureProvider), QQuickWindow::AfterSynchronizingStage);
         m_textureProvider = nullptr;
     }
 
 #if HAVE_XCB_COMPOSITE
+#if HAVE_GLX || HAVE_EGL
+    QQuickWindow::RenderStage m_renderStage = QQuickWindow::NoStage;
+#endif
 
 #if HAVE_GLX && HAVE_EGL
     // only one (or none) should be set, but never both
